index 0000000..786ca37
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/document-workspace-local.md
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+Current structural remediation: a shared canonical four-section validator rejects missing/duplicate/unknown IDs, absent/blank titles and empty/whitespace bodies. Outline response, approval, draft transition, partial revision and export share these invariants. Draft seeding is limited to affected IDs; unrelated user evidence is preserved.
+
+Final bounded service addendum: the local mock-only API now uses createAnthropicGenerator with the existing Anthropic SDK/messages conversion and a host-injected client factory. Ordinary consultation is the Haiku candidate and complex/document is the Sonnet candidate; no live routing quality is certified. Existing-client generation is dormant and request retry is explicitly zero. Previous Vertex adapter remains available but the final role-flow fixture uses Anthropic. Human-authored one-case reference artifacts and the distinction from mock/live results are in ../service-finish/README.md. This additional connection has local 450-unit/type/lint/build/browser checks, not a new independent quality pass. Production and actual calls remain disabled.
+
+# Jev + generation model local workspace
+
+Independent-review remediation supersedes the historical follow-up below: facts/leave corrections archive and invalidate affected request/facts/grounds text and all approvals. Reapproval must re-run generation with corrected structured facts, missing applicability data, issues, correction history, original notices and selected public evidence. Unrelated evidence text/IDs remain unchanged. Fresh generation is pending human review-only output approval; Word/documentText and PDF controls block unreviewed output. Model review does not certify legal correctness. Host-registered offline model factory/fetch are required; flags alone cannot invoke SDK/providers. Jev gets the registered fetch explicitly. Official Jev 1.13 pricing was checked on 2026-10-12: input $0.042 per million tokens, output free (https://docs.typesafe.ai/models). The output-fee objection is withdrawn. Mock-only gating remains because actual quality and paid-call approval are pending; no real usage or billing is measured. New unit count is 421/48 files. Current remediation evidence is ../quality-mix-revision-evidence/REVIEW-RESPONSE.md; old Library attachments are not passing artifacts and are not replaced.
+
+Latest follow-up: UI/API now call engine.ts with existingVertexGenerator and the budget-wrapped original Jev adapter; mock substitution is at SDK/fetch transport, not a canned API generator. The separate 3180 runtime records these transport calls with network blocked. Production remains disabled and the API additionally requires AI_WORKSPACE_MOCK_TRANSPORT=true. No live model IDs/rates have been selected.
+
+Reported headcount and leave corrections have separate audit fields; an 8 -> 4 report invalidates applicability/fact/outline approval, requests missing assessment data and never establishes statutory headcount by current count alone. Notices, other sections and evidence IDs are retained; reapproval retains prior text. BudgetRepository/RpcBudgetRepository and an unexecuted SQL proposal are added; real DB concurrency/permission checks remain unperformed. Eight-process local contention, mock RPC races and correction/output tests bring the unit total to 420/48 files. PDF overlay fixed; LibreOffice rendered DOCX end-to-end as a one-page alternative to untested Word application layout. Later report details supersede historical counts and architecture below.
+
+This is a local, disabled-by-default implementation for one synthetic dismissal case. It is not a commercial release or proof of Pro writing quality.
+
+## Source and boundaries
+
+Based on master 46bea61e782b2f970ff83a54720ab0d3e85758e9. PR27 was open/draft at 64375d6bfda7cde196fdc50d6570be3547f223d6. Its public-law-rerank.ts and exact public-law-manifest.json were copied into this separate local worktree; no ref, commit, push, merge, deployment or DB operation was performed. The original dirty checkout was preserved. The cancelled bounded-subset.patch was NOT applied.
+
+Library materialization of all four provided inputs failed. One PC-local retry used the unmodified official helper, which downloaded but could not apply required metadata because Python on Windows has no os.setxattr. No final file existed to read, no hash verification of the patch occurred, and no alternative transfer bypass was used. Thus the source plans and benchmarking document were not read locally. Their numbers are not claimed as achieved results.
+
+## Flow
+
+Local /ai/workspace shows the fixed synthetic case. Consultation creates separate facts, missing facts, issues and public evidence candidates. Explicit fact confirmation unlocks outline generation; explicit outline approval unlocks draft generation. The immutable structured Workspace has an independent revision and section IDs. Partial revision replaces only the selected section; other sections retain their exact text. Browser state is session-only: reload starts a new workspace. Word export uses real OOXML with Korean text, escaped XML, A4 dimensions and paragraph boundaries. PDF export invokes the browser print/save path with print-only document styling; automated validation uses Edge's Chromium PDF renderer. Microsoft Word itself was not opened for layout validation.
+
+The route is available only with AI_WORKSPACE_DEMO=true in development. It returns 404 in production regardless of the flag. There is no marketing link, no homepage redesign and no live route to generation. The API accepts a bounded body, same-origin loopback requests, the fixed synthetic case schema and legal evidence IDs. It never reads API keys or accepts attachments.
+
+## Model responsibilities
+
+Jev: public provenance-bound law selection only. selectPublicLawEvidence wraps the existing PR27 adapter in a persistent reservation. It receives the literal dismissal topic and verified public law rows, never case facts, the consultation text, document body or attachments. Missing/invalid public preparation preserves ordinary order. The existing adapter remains independently off by default and never impersonates Jev with Gemini fallback. The local browser demo uses an explicitly labelled Jev contract fixture rather than live Jev.
+
+Generation: ordinary, complex and document policies are separate. The local route dispatches consultation to fixture-ordinary, outline to fixture-complex, drafting to fixture-document. Their synthetic caps are 2048/4096/8192 respectively. The existing main chat's 1200 output cap is verified in stream-round.ts and remains unchanged; the new document path has its own cap. No cheap real model was selected. Actual policies must supply reviewed model IDs, conservative price rates and bounds; absence fails closed. existingVertexGenerator supports the existing Vertex provider and chosen model ID without adding a provider. It rejects truncated/blocked responses and accounts for total minus prompt tokens, including hidden thinking. It is not called by the demo.
+
+## Cost safety
+
+BudgetStore uses a private persistent ledger with an exclusive process-shared filesystem lock and atomic file replacement. Integer micro-USD reservations precede every provider start. Duplicate request IDs, monthly exposure over cap, unreadable/corrupt storage and stale locks deny new calls. Missing storage after initialization also denies rather than resetting. Pending and unknown previous-month reservations carry into the new month's exposure. The ledger stores only opaque request IDs, month, model, call count, token counts when authoritative, cost/reservation, latency and success/abstention/unknown state; no prompts, responses or attached source material.
+
+Timeouts and provider errors keep the maximum reservation. There is no automatic fallback or retry. An AbortSignal is not taken as proof that an SDK stopped billing; late completion after timeout cannot release reservation. Confirmed bounded usage may settle a generating request. PR27 does not expose usage/status, so Jev keeps the full maximum even on a returned result. This is conservative accounting, not measured actual spend. Fixture prices and monthly cap are test units, not a pricing recommendation.
+
+The filesystem store only coordinates processes sharing the same directory. It is not a verified distributed or serverless budget database. Production activation remains blocked; a durable shared atomic implementation and approval are required before a multi-replica rollout. Unknown Jev usage reconciliation is also pending.
+
+## Reproduce locally
+
+From the parent task workspace, node quality-mix-runtime.cjs dev starts localhost:3177 using isolated fake environment values, empty HOME and complete SDK fixtures. Visit http://127.0.0.1:3177/ai/workspace. No real .env file should be copied. The helper writes logs into quality-mix-evidence and runs only a temporary local process. node quality-mix-browser.cjs runs desktop/mobile Edge flows with external requests blocked. node quality-mix-check.cjs all, types, lint and lint-all run sanitized checks. node quality-mix-runtime.cjs build uses a distinct build directory. Existing dependencies are reused through a junction; no installation or package/lock changes.
+
+## Validation and remaining work
+
+415 unit tests across 46 files passed, including 32 new workflow/budget/Jev/Vertex fixture tests. Type and all new/copied TypeScript lint checks passed. Full lint remains 9 errors / 20 warnings in unchanged existing files. Fixture production build passed. Three browser cases passed: complete desktop flow, complete mobile flow, and real route invalid-state rejection. Word and PDF artifacts exist; PDF text extraction confirmed Korean and the revised section, two pages in the checked desktop artifact. PDF output button wiring was tested separately from PDF renderer output.
+
+Real provider calls: zero. Original case-law worker files/processes, SITEMAP_CASELAW, case noindex policy, original data, credentials, DB/migrations and production settings were not touched. Actual retrieval quality, model quality, Pro comparison, real cost, Word desktop layout and production suitability are untested. The Library helper incompatibility and unavailable reviewed patch remain explicit blockers for incorporating those inputs. Remote update is owned by the parent.
